    <section class="py-16 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">Frequently asked questions about BSL-2 and BSL-3 container laboratories</h2>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What is the difference between BSL-2 and BSL-3 in a container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-2 laboratories work with risk-group 2 pathogens and require a biosafety cabinet, autoclaves and controlled access. BSL-3 laboratories additionally require negative pressure, HEPA filtration, airlocks and gas-tight penetrations. Both levels can be implemented in <a href="/en/services/modular-construction" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">container construction</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                How long does it take to realise a BSL container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A BSL-2 container laboratory can be realised within a few months — considerably faster than a conventional new build. BSL-3 projects take somewhat longer because of more complex permit procedures, but are still faster than solid construction. More on the <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-project-process" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">project process</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Which permits do I need for a BSL container laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">For BSL-2 a notification to the competent authority is generally sufficient. BSL-3 requires a permit under the Biological Agents Ordinance (BioStoffV). Building-law permits come on top — all of this is covered in our <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-permits-building-law" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">permits guide</a>. Our <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">consulting</a> accompanies you through the process.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Can a BSL container laboratory change site?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes, that is one of the great advantages over solid construction. A BSL container laboratory can be dismantled, transported and recommissioned at a new site — the entire certified unit remains intact. More on <a href="/en/services/logistics" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">logistics &amp; installation</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What technical equipment belongs in a BSL-2/BSL-3 laboratory?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-2 requires at least biosafety cabinets, autoclaves, eyewash, emergency shower and controlled access. BSL-3 additionally requires HEPA filtration, negative-pressure ventilation systems, gas-tight penetrations and airlocks. Details are in our <a href="/en/magazine/lab-container-equipment-checklist" class="text-[#5c7300] hover:underline">equipment checklist</a>.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Is a BSL-3 container laboratory as safe as a conventional one?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Yes. Modern container laboratories meet exactly the same safety requirements as conventional BSL-3 laboratories. Controlled workshop manufacture even offers quality advantages, because all installations are fitted and tested under optimal conditions.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What does BSL mean?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL stands for biosafety level, the internationally used classification of laboratories by infection risk in four levels. In German law this corresponds to the protection level under the Biological Agents Ordinance (section 5 BioStoffV) and, for genetic engineering, to safety levels S1 to S4 under section 7 of the Genetic Engineering Act.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                What is the UK equivalent of BSL-3?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Containment Level 3 under COSHH Schedule 3 Part II. Compared with Level 2 it requires HEPA-filtered extract air, a workplace sealable for disinfection, negative pressure to atmosphere and an observation window.</div>
            </details>
            <details class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden group">
              <summary class="flex items-center justify-between p-6 cursor-pointer font-bold text-slate-900 hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                Does a BSL-3 laboratory need an airlock?
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-primary transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">In the UK, COSHH Schedule 3 requires an air-lock only at Containment Level 4. In Germany, TRBA 100 requires an anteroom with two self-closing, interlocked doors for protection level 3.</div>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
